---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "~/components/common/container.astro";
import { ArrowLeft } from "lucide-astro";
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    

    <Container>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <a href="/" class="text-muted-foreground flex items-center pt-2"
          ><ArrowLeft size={16} className="mr-1.5" /> Back to works</a
        >
        <h1 class="uppercase text-3xl font-serif font-medium pb-6">SUPERBAI</h1>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-12  md:flex-row items-start justify-between ">
        <div class="md:w-1/2">
          <div class="flex gap-6 md:gap-12 flex-col">
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h2 class="text-lg font-serif uppercase font-medium">Timeline</h2>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">2 months</p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h2 class="text-lg font-serif uppercase font-medium">Live</h2>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">[REDACTED]</p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h2 class="text-lg font-serif uppercase font-medium">Tech</h2>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">nextjs, firestore, trpc</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="md:w-1/2">
          <div class="flex gap-6 md:gap-12 flex-col">
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h2 class="text-lg font-serif uppercase font-medium">Overview</h2>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">An internal dashboard for SUPERBAI's operations team to register maids, search by service and location, and manage admin records — replacing a workflow that ran on messages, spreadsheets, and memory.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-1">
              <h2 class="text-lg font-serif uppercase font-medium">Problems Solved</h2>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">Maid registration was scattered across group chats and spreadsheets with no single source of truth. Finding the right maid for a request meant manually cross-referencing service type, time slot, and location. No consistent system for managing admin users and internal operational data.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      </div>
      
    </Container>

    <Container>
      <article class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif uppercase font-medium">Product screenshots</h2>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 mb-12">
          <figure>
            <img
              class="rounded"
              data-lightbox
              src="/images/superbai/dashboard-main.png"
              alt="SUPERBAI dashboard overview showing internal collections and operational records"
            />
            <figcaption class="sr-only">
              The main dashboard view keeps SUPERBAI's internal operations organized around clear collections.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure>
            <img
              class="rounded"
              data-lightbox
              src="/images/superbai/dashboard-add-maid.png"
              alt="SUPERBAI add maid screen with a structured registration form"
            />
            <figcaption class="sr-only">
              Maid registration was designed as a structured form, not another loose operational checklist.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure>
            <img
              class="rounded"
              data-lightbox
              src="/images/superbai/dashboard-maid-search.png"
              alt="SUPERBAI maid search module with filters for service, time slot, and location"
            />
            <figcaption class="sr-only">
              The maid search module turns service, time, and location constraints into a focused lookup workflow.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure>
            <img
              class="rounded"
              data-lightbox
              src="/images/superbai/dashboard-admin.png"
              alt="SUPERBAI admin collection screen for managing internal users"
            />
            <figcaption class="sr-only">
              Admin management follows the same collection pattern, keeping future internal workflows consistent.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

      </article>
    </Container>

    <Container>
    </Container>
  </main>
</Layout>
